Aim

To integrate JUnit test cases with Jenkins and run automated tests to view test reports.

Theory (Short)

JUnit is used to write unit test cases for Java applications.
Jenkins is a CI tool that automatically builds the project and runs JUnit tests.
The Jenkins pipeline fetches code from GitHub, runs Maven tests, and generates test reports.

Steps
Step 1: Create Maven Project
mvn archetype:generate

Enter:

GroupId: com.devops.lab
ArtifactId: lab13-junit-jenkins
Packaging: jar
Archetype: maven-archetype-quickstart
Step 2: Add Calculator.java

Location:

src/main/java/com/devops/lab/Calculator.java

(Add same Calculator code)

Step 3: Add CalculatorTest.java

Location:

src/test/java/com/devops/lab/CalculatorTest.java

(Add JUnit test cases)

Step 4: Update pom.xml

Add:

JUnit dependency
Maven Surefire plugin
Step 5: Run Maven Test
mvn clean test

Check:

target/surefire-reports
Step 6: Push Code to GitHub
git init
git add .
git commit -m "JUnit Jenkins Lab"
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/lab13.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
Step 7: Create Jenkins Pipeline

Create Jenkinsfile

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git 'https://github.com/username/lab13.git'
            }
        }

        stage('Build & Test') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn clean test'
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            junit '**/target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
        }
    }
}
